Revision history for Game-Schnapsen

0.03    2026-10-11
        - Add Game::Schnapsen::Terminal->run(@argv), which returns the exit status
        - A bad option or a refused value is exit status 2, not 1
        - Fix: rank_text had no POD, so t/pod-coverage.t failed

0.02    2026-10-10
        - Point at the card you mean: the arrow keys walk your hand and the
          line under it says whether the card takes the trick, what the trick
          is worth, and what that puts you on. The moves that are not cards
          keep their own keys.
        - The card you drew at the end of the last trick is drawn in a
          heavier frame.
        - Fix: --level took any number. The variant, the mode and the seat
          were all refused; the level was not.
        - Fix: every drawn row ended in the padding that keeps the next card
          in line.
        - Fix: the hand's label row padded by the length of a string that
          already held colour codes, so with colour on, which is the default
          on a terminal, the labels did not line up under their cards.
        - The ten is drawn as 10 rather than T. T is the engine's rank
          letter, which keeps a card id two characters; it was never a
          thing to show a player. Both spellings are still accepted.
        - Fix: an answer or a refusal landed on the prompt's own line off a
          terminal.

0.01    2026-09-15
        First version.
